\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 time.sleep(random.uniform(1, 3))
\f1\b0\fs24 : Before making the actual request, the script pauses for a random duration between 1 and 3 seconds. This helps to mimic human browsing behavior (humans don't click instantly) and can help avoid rate-limiting or bot detection that flags overly consistent or rapid requests.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 webpage = requests.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=15)
\f1\b0\fs24 : This is the core of the request.\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl2
\f2\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 requests.get(url)
\f1\fs24 : Sends an HTTP GET request to the specified 
\f2\fs26 url
\f1\fs24 .\
\ls4\ilvl2
\f2\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 headers=headers
\f1\fs24 : Attaches the custom 
\f2\fs26 headers
\f1\fs24  dictionary we defined earlier to the request.\
\ls4\ilvl2
\f2\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 timeout=15
\f1\fs24 : This is very important. It sets a maximum waiting time (in seconds) for the server to send a response. If the server doesn't respond within 15 seconds, a 
\f2\fs26 requests.exceptions.Timeout
\f1\fs24  error is raised, preventing your script from hanging indefinitely.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 webpage.raise_for_status()
\f1\b0\fs24 : After receiving a response, this method checks if the HTTP status code indicates an error (i.e., a 4xx client error or 5xx server error). If it does, it raises an 
\f2\fs26 HTTPError
\f1\fs24  exception. This is a quick way to catch issues like 
\f2\fs26 403 Forbidden
\f1\fs24  or 
\f2\fs26 404 Not Found
\f1\fs24 .\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 print("Page content successfully retrieved!")
\f1\b0\fs24 : If the request is successful and no HTTP error occurs, this message is printed.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 print(webpage.text[:500])
\f1\b0\fs24 : 
\f2\fs26 webpage.text
\f1\fs24  contains the entire HTML content of the fetched page as a string. We print only the first 500 characters to confirm that we received HTML data without cluttering the output.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 except requests.exceptions.Timeout as e:
\f1\b0\fs24 : This block catches the 
\f2\fs26 Timeout
\f1\fs24  exception, which occurs if the server doesn't respond within the specified 
\f2\fs26 timeout
\f1\fs24  duration.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 except requests.exceptions.HTTPError as e:
\f1\b0\fs24 : This block catches 
\f2\fs26 HTTPError
\f1\fs24  exceptions, which are raised by 
\f2\fs26 raise_for_status()
\f1\fs24  for bad HTTP status codes (like the 
\f2\fs26 403 Forbidden
\f1\fs24  you encountered earlier). It also prints the specific status code and a snippet of the server's error response.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 except requests.exceptions.ConnectionError as e:
\f1\b0\fs24 : This catches errors related to network connectivity issues (e.g., DNS resolution failure, host unreachable).\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f3\b\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:
\f1\b0\fs24 : This is a general catch-all for any other exception that might occur during the 
\f2\fs26 requests
\f1\fs24  operation. 
\f2\fs26 RequestException
\f1\fs24  is the base class for all exceptions in the 
\f2\fs26 requests
\f1\fs24  library.\
